/P 231 0 R
/E (Onera is a medical-grade, patch-based sleep testing platform designed to make polysomnography more accessible outside the lab. Instead of dozens of wires, Onera uses wireless patches placed on the chest, forehead, and legs to capture many of the same signals as an in-lab study. We are able to measure EEG \(brain waves\), EOG \(eye movement\), EMG \(muscle tone\), breathing effort, airflow, leg movement, body position and heart rate.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
